RF.put("questb:b50",{"8690":{"id":8690,"t":"Cloak of the Gathering Storm","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 1 Qiraji Regal Drape, 2 Obsidian Idols, 5 Clay Scarabs and 5 Gold Scarabs to Keyl Swiftclaw in Silithus. You must also obtain Revered reputation with Cenarion Circle to complete this quest.\nQiraji Regal Drape General Rajaxx 40 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Kurinnaxx 40 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Ayamiss the Hunter 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Buru the Gorger 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj\n2 Obsidian Idol Flesh Hunter 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Drone 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Collector 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Soldier 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj and 4 more\n5 Clay Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Gold Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 21000 reputation with Cenarion Circle","desc":"I'm glad to hear you're aiding us in our attack on Ahn'Qiraj, ‹name›. I can make you a protective item that'll be of assistance in the fight against our enemy, ‹class›.\nI shall need a Qiraji drape, which I'll resize for you of course. I'll also need idols and scarabs which I'll use to create a suitable clasp.\nI promise you won't be disappointed.","rew":"You will receive:\nCloak of the Gathering Storm\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Did you bring the materials for the cloak, ‹name›?","done":"Ah yes... this drape is immaculate.\nTake this cloak, ‹name›. May it protect you from the foul magic of the Qiraji.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":51.8,"y":39.5,"n":"Keyl Swiftclaw","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8610":{"id":8610,"t":"The Horde Needs More Runecloth Bandages!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 20 Runecloth Bandages to Stoneguard Clayhoof at the Valley of Spirits in Orgrimmar.\n20 Runecloth Bandage","desc":"Ever does the time grow nearer when we shall launch ourselves headlong into the conflagration at Ahn'Qiraj, priest. But first we must gather our strength and prepare so that we can survive the onslaught of the insects and their masters.\nIf you are here again, then surely you wish to make another contribution of runecloth bandages to the war effort? Please do so as soon as you can and return to me once more.","rew":"You will receive:\n10 Horde Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","done":"It is a very selfless act of giving that you perform, ‹name›. One that is likely to save the lives of many combatants at Ahn'Qiraj. Thank you and know that you have the appreciation of the Horde for your donation. Should you create, or come across, more runecloth bandages, please consider bringing them to me here.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":31.6,"y":75.8,"n":"Stoneguard Clayhoof","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"8850":{"id":8850,"t":"Thirty Signets for War Supplies","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"30 Alliance Commendation Signet","rew":"You will receive:\nAhn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":60.5,"y":34.7,"n":"Field Marshal Snowfall","s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"8530":{"id":8530,"t":"The alliance needs singed corestones","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Bring 50 singed corestones to Commander Stronghammer at the airfield in Dun Morogh.\n50 Singed Corestone","desc":"‹class›, I need your help. In the Molten Core there are these stones, singed Corestones to be precise, that we need to harvest for the Ahn'Qiraj war effort. I'm told that our blacksmiths and engineers can put them to good use, so that's where you come in. I need you to go into the Molten Core and gather up as many of these corestones as you can. Of course, you'll want to talk thirty-nine of your closest friends along with you.\nLevel 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Type Raid Shareable Yes Quest ID 8530","cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"7170":{"id":7170,"t":"Earned Reverence","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Stormpike Insignia Rank 3","desc":"I must know, ‹name›. When you look directly into the eyes of the enemy, do you see fear? Do they now cower in your presence? They must realize that they are defeated!\nYou have earned reverence among the Guard.\nPresent your insignia!","rew":"You will receive:\nStormpike Insignia Rank 4\nExperience: 8,300\n+150 reputation with Stormpike Guard\n+150 reputation with Ironforge","back":"I must know, ‹name›. When you look directly into the eyes of the enemy, do you see fear? Do they now cower in your presence? They must realize that they are defeated!\nYou have earned reverence among the Guard. Present your insignia!","done":"When we first met, I would have never guessed that a hero was in the making. Carry on, soldier!","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":39.5,"y":81.2,"n":"Lieutenant Haggerdin","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["alterac-valley"]},"8370":{"id":8370,"t":"Conquering Arathi Basin","lv":29,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Arathi Basin Mark of Honor to a Horde Warbringer outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Arathi Basin Mark of Honor","desc":"Our conflict with the Alliance has escalated to a true war. No longer are false pretenses to enter into battle used or expected by either side at this point.\nThe battle for the Arathi Basin is one of resources, plain and simple. Either the Alliance gets the resources and uses them against us or we get them and use them to keep our war efforts going. Help the Defilers maintain the flow of resources we need, ‹name›!","rew":"Money: 25 0 gold, 25 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,350\n+100 reputation with The Defilers","back":"You've come back with news from Arathi, ‹class›?","done":"Securing our resources in Arathi is an important task! You've done well, ‹name›.\nThe Barrens Arathi Highlands Undercity","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":46.7,"y":8.7,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":73.5,"y":29.1,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":58.3,"y":97.9,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-basin"]},"1010":{"id":1010,"t":"Bathran's Hair","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 5 Bathran's Hair to Orendil Broadleaf in Ashenvale.\n5 Bathran's Hair Plant Bundle","desc":"There is a plant that once grew in the old ruins of Bathran's Haunt to the north. The plant was called Bathran's Hair and was known to cure ailments of the spirit.\nThere is a sick child in the village, and I believe it is more than just a physical illness. Will you go to Bathran's Haunt and search it for Bathran's Hair? I may need it to properly treat the child.\nBathran's Haunt lies north of Maestra's Post and just south of the border to Darkshore.","rew":"Experience: 775\n+50 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Have you gathered the Bathran's Hair, ‹name›? The child's health grows weaker by the hour...","done":"Ah, you have the hair! Now I will mix a cure for the child, and pray my concoction works.\nAnd... Forsaken are at Bathran's Haunt? Very troubling to hear, that is. Very troubling indeed...","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":26.4,"y":38.6,"n":"Orendil Broadleaf","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"79090":{"id":79090,"t":"Repelling invaders","lv":60,"min":18,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring the Warsong Outrider Mark to Felore Moonray, Priestess of the Moon, at the Moonwell base in Ashenvale.\nProvided: Warsong Outrider Mark","desc":"Some of the Warsong Outriders lie defeated, but the battle still rages...","rew":"You will receive:\nItem 211815\n+1,000 reputation with Silverwing Sentinels\n0 reputation with Stormwind\n0 reputation with Darnassus","back":"‹name›, what news do you have from the front?","done":"These Horde invaders still sully our lands and harvest from our sacred wilderness. Continue to drive them out!\nThis sacred battle hymn may inspire you to fight them with greater determination. Thank you, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":60,"y":72.6,"n":"Felore Moonray","e":1},{"z":"Ashenvale","x":36.8,"y":49.6,"n":"Felore Moonray","e":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"7650":{"id":7650,"t":"Enchanted Thorium Platemail: Volume II","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 50 instead of 60. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 14,500, 0.46 times as much.","obj":"Return the book to its rightful owners.\nEnchanted Thorium Platemail\nProvided: Enchanted Thorium Platemail","desc":"The tome carries the mark of the Athenaeum.","rew":"You will receive:\nPlans: Enchanted Thorium Leggings\nExperience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with Shen'dralar","back":"You have recovered a tome!","done":"Well done, my boy.\n<Lorekeeper Lydros tears out a page from the book.>\nI am sure you can make use of this recipe.\nStart an item: Enchanted Thorium Platemail End Lorekeeper Lydros Level 60 , requires level 50 Difficulty 50 56 58 Side Both factions Type Dungeon Profession Blacksmithing 300 Shareable No Quest ID 7650","cats":["blacksmithing"]},"96050":{"id":96050,"t":"Camping 101 fishing","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Paxton Ganter near Iceflow Lake in Dun Morogh to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your fishing skill to 20","desc":"You might not think so, but your skill as a fisherman can actually come in handy at camp.\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Fish Bowl for your camp. You can use this fixture to help provide a bit of joy to yourself and your fellow adventurers. A happy adventurer is a strong adventurer and I'm sure your combat capabilities will reflect that.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own Fish Bowl. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":46.6,"y":53.8,"n":"Eric Brighthammer","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":35.4,"y":40.2,"n":"Paxton Ganter","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"97970":{"id":97970,"t":"Camping 101 mining","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Messana Crestwind in Shen'dar Village to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your mining skill to 20","desc":"Mining isn't the most glamorous, but it's good honest work and a fine profession for you to explore.\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Lodestone for your camp. Build one of these and everyone who wants to swing a sword will be eager to gather round your fire and soak up the extra \"oomph\" it can provide to increase their combat prowess.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own Lodestone. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":41.6,"y":44.8,"n":"Raan Wildwind","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":44.8,"y":44.4,"n":"Messana Crestwind","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"6610":{"id":6610,"t":"Clamlette Surprise","lv":45,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Dirge Quikcleave wants you to get the following items:\n12 Giant Eggs. You will find those on the Rocs wandering Tanaris or any other species of large bird.\n10 pieces of Zesty Clam Meat. You can find those in clams, naturally!\n20 pieces of Alterac Swiss. Get thee to a cheesery!\nGather all of the items and return to Dirge.\n12 Giant Egg Ironbeak Screecher 48 % , Ironbeak Hunter 47 % , Ironbeak Owl 45.2 % , Winterspring Owl 44.6 % and 4 more\n10 Zesty Clam Meat\n20 Alterac Swiss Skeletal Servant , Supply Crate 93.2 % in Stratholme , General Marcus Jonathan 71.4 % , Vengeful Phantom 60 % in Stratholme and 4 more","desc":"Ever heard of a clamlette? Of course you haven't! It's my latest and greatest culinary masterpiece. Oh, ‹name›, just thinking about a clamlette makes my mouth water.\nUnfortunately, I'm all out of supplies to make any! How about I make you a deal? You gather the supplies I need to make a clamlette and I'll teach you the finer points of exotic cuisine and I'll even throw in a couple of clamlettes to boot! Deal??\nHere's what I need:","rew":"You will receive:\n20 Clamlette Surprise\nYou will learn: Cooking\nExperience: 3,900","back":"My cravings are going to be the end of me! Hurry, ‹name› - before I dip into my own supply.","done":"You are in for a special treat, ‹name›. Watch and learn!\n<Dirge begins to prepare clamlette surprise.>","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":52.6,"y":28.1,"n":"Dirge Quikcleave","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["cooking"]},"94290":{"id":94290,"t":"Craftsmans writ mechanical repair kit","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Mechanical Repair Kit\nMechanical Repair Kit","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Mechanical Repair Kit, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Mechanical Repair Kit Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94290","cats":["crafting"]},"7890":{"id":7890,"t":"Heavy Grinding Stone","lv":60,"min":10,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"7 Heavy Grinding Stone","rew":"You will receive:\n4 Darkmoon Faire Prize Ticket\n+100 reputation with Darkmoon Faire","back":"To help with my workout, I like to fit a staff between heavy grinding stones, then lift the staff over my head. It isn't easy, but being the strongest woman in the world, like I am, can't be earned sitting down!\nCan you help me? I need more grinding stones - bring me some and I'll trade Darkmoon Faire tickets for them.","done":"You brought the stones! And they're heavy! I can already feel my muscles getting bigger. Thanks ‹name›!\nHere, take these tickets, and be sure not to eat too many sweets while your at the faire. A big strong ‹class› like you needs to keep himself in fighting shape!\nMulgore Elwynn Forest","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":38.6,"y":46.4,"n":"Kerri Hicks","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":40.5,"y":69.9,"n":"Kerri Hicks","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkmoon-faire"]},"6130":{"id":6130,"t":"Power over Poison","lv":14,"min":14,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return to Turak Runetotem on the Elder Rise, Thunder Bluff.","desc":"You've learned what it means to cure poison without the benefit of spiritual aid. Remember what others must endure in fighting poisonous afflictions as you soon embrace your newfound power over poison.\nYou should now return to Turak Runetotem in Thunder Bluff, ‹name›. He, no doubt, has a very important spell to teach you now that the student understands the lesson given unto him/her.\nFarewell, young druid. We shall speak again.","rew":"You will learn: Cure Poison\nExperience: 975\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","done":"Welcome back - I've been following your progress on this lesson since you left, and I must admit I was surprised to learn about the situation at the Crossroads. This does bear some further investigation, as the introduction of such poisons into the environment is most upsetting to the balance.\nYou handled yourself with grace under pressure. For that, I can find no better way to reward you with permanent power over poison. Use it well, ‹name›... use it well.\nMoonglade Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"Moonglade","x":56.2,"y":30.6,"n":"Dendrite Starblaze","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":76.5,"y":27.2,"n":"Turak Runetotem","e":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"1170":{"id":1170,"t":"The Brood of Onyxia","lv":43,"min":38,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Overlord Mok'Morokk in Brackenwall Village.","desc":"Stonemaul Village was invaded by the brood of Onyxia. But why would the daughter of the black dragonlord, Deathwing, descend upon our lands?\nThis is most troubling. Surely, Onyxia was driven here for a purpose beyond laying siege to a small band of ogres.\nNotify Mok'Morokk at once! Action must be taken.","rew":"Experience: 360","done":"Why you tell me 'bout dragons? Me no like dragons. Me like it here. No dragons here.","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":37.2,"y":33.1,"n":"Draz'Zilb","s":1},{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":36.3,"y":31.4,"n":"Overlord Mok'Morokk","e":1}],"cats":["dustwallow-marsh"]},"8930":{"id":8930,"t":"In Search of Anthion","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use the Extra-Dimensional Ghost Revealer at the entrance to Stratholme and speak with the ghost of Anthion Harmon.\nProvided: Extra-Dimensional Ghost Revealer","desc":"Very well, ‹name›. All that remains is to put the goblin's invention to the test. Word has it that Anthion was slain by the undead legions of Stratholme as he tried to enter its gates.\nTry using the device there and see if, indeed, you can speak with the dead!","rew":"Experience: 6,600","done":"Mokvar had you contact me? I'll do my best to help you, but first I must ask a great favor of you.\nOrgrimmar Eastern Plaguelands","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":34.9,"y":38.3,"n":"Mokvar","s":1},{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":26.1,"y":11.3,"n":"Anthion Harmon","e":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"95810":{"id":95810,"t":"Lost relic carry","lv":31,"min":24,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring the Titan Relic to Prospector Whelgar in the Wetlands excavation site.\nTitan Relic","desc":"You pick up a fractured piece of the rock-mech automaton. It has a texture unlike anything you've touched before, a composite material of unknown makeup. This is certainly bound to be more 'device' than 'debris.'\nProspector Whelgar himself at his excavation site might have something useful to share about the relic.","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":38.8,"y":52.2,"n":"Prospector Whelgar","e":1}],"cats":["excavation-site-wetlands-dungeon"]},"5890":{"id":5890,"t":"Salve via Skinning","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"5 Patch of Tainted Skin","rew":"You will receive:\n2 Cenarion Plant Salve\nExperience: 4,200","back":"A Cenarion beacon will allow a well-trained skinner to spot patches of tainted skin from bounty gathered in Felwood. I convert these seemingly useless patches into a thick paste that serves as a quickening agent for Cenarion plant salve. When you skin your kills here in Felwood, be sure to have a beacon on you!\nWhen you collect tainted patches, bring them to me and I will give you some Cenarion plant salves that I have already made.","done":"This is exactly what I need. Here - take these plant salves and use them to reclaim Felwood from the corruption. We must persevere, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":46.7,"y":83.1,"n":"Maybess Riverbreeze","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"4130":{"id":4130,"t":"Psychometric Reading","lv":44,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Ginro Hearthkindle in Feathermoon Stronghold.","desc":"I'm a little wobbly still, sorry. Anyway, I received some useful visions.\nRaschal takes two large leather backpacks from his boat and goes inland; he returns to the boat, however. I see gnoll scalps... he ran into some gnolls - Woodpaw I think they're called. He's very worried - almost terrified - about something. So much so, that he is not paying attention to water elementals forming behind him. The images... stop there.\nI need to rest, sorry ‹name›. Tell Gin what I've seen. He needs to know.","rew":"Experience: 380","done":"Thanks for passing along Quint's visions to me, ‹name›. I'll try to remember to be a little easier on him the next time we play cards.\nRaschal can hold his own in a fight, and gnolls aren't anything that would get him worried - nay, terrified. Still, maybe you and yours can act on this new information and make the breakthrough we desperately need.","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":32.4,"y":43.8,"n":"Quintis Jonespyre","s":1},{"z":"Feralas","x":31.9,"y":45.1,"n":"Ginro Hearthkindle","e":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"7730":{"id":7730,"t":"Zukk'ash Infestation","lv":45,"min":39,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 20 Zukk'ash Carapaces to Hadoken Swiftstrider at Camp Mojache, Feralas.\n20 Zukk'ash Carapace Zukk'ash Stinger , Zukk'ash Wasp , Zukk'ash Worker , Zukk'ash Tunneler and 1 more","desc":"From what scouting we have managed to muster, we believe that the foe south of the gnolls is an insect-like race. Frankly, it is irrelevant whether or not if they're sentient. If they are driving the gnolls to frenzy against us, then they are as big of a threat - if not more - than the gnolls.\nDrive deep into where these Zukk'ash insects dwell; it is known as the Writhing Deep. Thin their numbers and report back to me what you find, bringing back their carapaces as evidence of your handiwork.","rew":"Money: 65 0 gold, 65 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,900\n+100 reputation with Horde","back":"How goes the hunt, ‹name›? Are you here to report your success?","done":"Well done, ‹class›. Though the extensiveness of the Zukk'ash presence will not be thwarted with anything less than a full-scale invasion, you have bought us some time so we can devise a proper strategy.\nI will be sure to have these carapaces analyzed; we'll need to learn everything about them before we deal with what has unfortunately turned into a much larger issue than we had anticipated.","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":74.9,"y":42.5,"n":"Hadoken Swiftstrider","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"2930":{"id":2930,"t":"Data Rescue","lv":30,"min":25,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring a Prismatic Punch Card to Master Mechanic Castpipe in Ironforge.\nPrismatic Punch Card","desc":"When we fled Gnomeregan, we left so much data behind! Vitally important data!\nI need the data on a prismatic punch card, from a Matrix Punchograph 3005-D high security terminal, deep in Gnomeregan. You must access the terminal, but to do that you first need clearance... and to get that you must access lower security terminals-- models -A, -B and -C. And to do THAT you need security punch cards, starting with white... and we left all the punch cards in the city.\nIt's a catastrophe! Can you help?","rew":"You will receive:\nRepairman's Cape Mechanic's Pipehammer\nMoney: 25 0 gold, 25 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,650\n+200 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"Do you have the prismatic punch card??","done":"You did it! You found the prismatic punch card and recovered the lost data! Vitally, critically, immeasurably important data that we could not live another moment without!\nYour service to the gnomes will be long remembered, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.3,"y":28.8,"n":"Master Mechanic Castpipe","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["gnomeregan"]},"94050":{"id":94050,"t":"Training the beast","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak to Quel'dora Quickgale in Valanaar.","desc":"You now have the power to tame a pet, but you must also gain the skills to train it. For this, there is none better than my sister, Quel'dora. She will give you the ability to train your new pet.\nGo with the winds, young ‹class›.","done":"A fledgling ‹class›, I see. Yes, I can bestow you with the skills you need to train and guide your pet. Not only will you be able to teach your pet new abilities, you will now be able to feed your pet, as well as revive it, should it fall in battle.\nRemember, Gei, always respect the balance and live in awe of nature around you. Now, go forth. We shall speak again, at a later date.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":59.6,"y":72.6,"n":"Quel'ana Quickgale","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":59.6,"y":72.6,"n":"Quel'dora Quickgale","e":1}],"cats":["hunter"]},"5090":{"id":5090,"t":"A Call to Arms: The Plaguelands!","lv":50,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Seek out Commander Ashlam Valorfist. His base camp is located at Chillwind Camp, north of the Alterac Mountains.","desc":"Hear ye, hear ye! All heroes are called upon to heed these words!\nA call to arms has been issued by the Kingdom of Stormwind! All able bodied individuals are entreated to take up arms against the dark threat of the Scourge in the northern lands of the Eastern Kingdoms! Rumors fly of new threats rising from the ruins of the Plaguelands!\nHeroes of the realm - seek out Commander Ashlam Valorfist who has set up his base camp in Chillwind Camp, north of the Alterac Mountains!","rew":"Experience: 470\n+10 reputation with Stormwind","done":"Welcome to the Plaguelands, hero. This is one of most dangerous frontiers in Azeroth, especially with the looming threat of the Scourge to our north and northeast. I am glad to hear that the clarion call of duty and service to the greater good did not fall on deaf ears with you!\nIf you are ready to get your hands dirty, then there is plenty for willing and able heroes to do here on the edge of the Plaguelands.\nDun Morogh Western Plaguelands","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":60.1,"y":34.2,"n":"Courier Hammerfall","s":1},{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":42.7,"y":84,"n":"Commander Ashlam Valorfist","e":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"2850":{"id":2850,"t":"Wild Leather Helmet","lv":45,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 2 Nightscape Tunics, 2 Nightscape Headbands, and a Wildvine to Pratt McGrubben in Feathermoon Stronghold.\n2 Nightscape Tunic\n2 Nightscape Headband\nWildvine Retherokk the Berserker 80.6 % , Zul'arek Hatefowler 65.1 % , Purple Lotus 10 % , Vilebranch Aman'zasi Guard 9.5 % and 4 more","desc":"A Wild Leather helmet offers the wearer superior protection to the vital areas of the head without a sacrifice in comfort. As with all Wild Leather armor, the integrated wildvine yields a powerful but random enhancement to the frame of the helm. Leather wearers will definitely want this piece!\nFor this pattern, I will need two Nightscape tunics, two Nightscape headbands, and a wildvine. Complete this order and the pattern will be yours!","rew":"You will receive:\nPattern: Wild Leather Helmet\nExperience: 2,900","back":"I need those tunics and headbands made, and I also need that piece of wildvine before I will share with you the knowledge of Wild Leather helmets.\nHead gear is highly coveted amongst adventurers, whether it be a disarmingly simple headband or a full-covering helmet. The fundamentals of creating valued head gear remain constant, no matter what the cosmetic appearance of the gear is.","done":"This Nightscape equipment you have supplied fills the order perfectly, ‹name›. I expect no less from a leatherworker of your caliber.\nYou have definitely earned this pattern. I give it to you freely, and hope you will profit from it accordingly.","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":30.6,"y":42.7,"n":"Pratt McGrubben","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["leatherworking"]},"9250":{"id":9250,"t":"Frame of Atiesh","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 9,550, 0.69 times as much.","obj":"Find someone that will help you in recovering the last two pieces of the staff and ridding it of evil.\nFrame of Atiesh\nProvided: Frame of Atiesh","desc":"With the frame formed, Atiesh is nearly whole. Only the head and base of the staff are now missing. There is also a minor issue regarding the staff being a conduit for Sargeras's evil.\nFind someone that can assist you in locating the remaining pieces and exorcising the evil from the staff.","rew":"Experience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"It was her time, mortal.","done":"The archmages have died.\nDo not mourn their passing, ‹name›. All such things are fated. Just as you holding the staff of the Guardian was fated...","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":65.3,"y":50,"n":"Anachronos","e":1}],"cats":["legendary"]},"9330":{"id":9330,"t":"Stealing Stormwind's Flame","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays 70s instead of 0. Gives 4,950 experience instead of 5,000, 0.99 times as much. New rewards: Fiery Festival Brew. No longer rewards Toasted Smorc, Midsummer Sausage, Fire-toasted Bun, Elderberry Pie.","obj":"Return the Flame of Stormwind to the Festival Talespinner.\nFlame of Stormwind\nProvided: Flame of Stormwind","desc":"This flame, stolen from the heart of Stormwind itself, floods you with warmth. This raw power is foreign to you, but the Talespinner might know more...","rew":"New in Forever: Fiery Festival Brew.\nYou will receive:\n20 Fiery Festival Brew 20 Burning Blossom\nMoney: 70 0 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,950","back":"You're practically glowing, ‹race›. What do you have there?","done":"And this brightly-burning fire... you say it came from Stormwind? Remarkable! That must have been quite an adventure! I'll pay you for this, of course. If you find anything else like this, be sure to speak with me again.\nThunder Bluff Orgrimmar Tirisfal Glades","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":21.5,"y":27.2,"n":"Festival Talespinner","e":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":42.8,"y":34.9,"n":"Festival Talespinner","e":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":61.9,"y":73.1,"n":"Festival Talespinner","e":1}],"cats":["midsummer"]},"96130":{"id":96130,"t":"Chakuyak","lv":5,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Defeat Chakuyak and bring back her pelt.\nChakuyak's Pelt","desc":"Among the prairie wolves that hunt the hills nearby is one that is especially aggressive. We have taken to calling her Chakuyak. She has become a threat to travelers coming from abroad.\nShe stalks the trees west of Stonebull Lake, moving from tree stand to tree stand.\nEnd this threat and bring me her pelt, and I will speak your praises to the chief. Beware, for she is dangerous! You might see other hunters seeking her out there, and perhaps you could work as a team.","rew":"You will receive:\nFurred Belt\nMoney: 50 0 gold, 0 silver, 50 copper Experience: 230\n+50 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Have you found the big wolf?","done":"Taking the life of such a beautiful creature is a sad event, but it was necessary for the safety of our people. I will make certain that the pelt does not go to waste. Thank you.","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":46.8,"y":59.6,"n":"Yaw Sharpmane","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"770":{"id":770,"t":"The Demon Scarred Cloak","lv":12,"min":6,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find someone who knows of Ghost Howl.\nProvided: Demon Scarred Cloak","desc":"The ragged hide of Ghost Howl still bears a terrible wound, gained from the wolf's battles against the Burning Legion.\nPerhaps someone in Bloodhoof Village should know of Ghost Howl's demise....","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSkorn's Hammer Skorn's Rifle\nExperience: 900\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","done":"I can barely believe my old eyes! You defeated the great wolf Ghost Howl? I look upon you with new respect, young ‹class›. You are a ‹class› of extreme skills!\nLet me offer you something. My days of hunting are over, but I would be honored if you used one of my weapons in your hunts.\nMay it strike true, and bring you renown.\nAnd let us hope that Ghost Howl's spirit has finally found peace.","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":46,"y":63.4,"n":"Skorn Whitecloud","e":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"9090":{"id":9090,"t":"Dreamwalker Boots","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Rayne at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make Dreamwalker Boots if you bring her the following: 1 Desecrated Boots, 12 Wartorn Leather Scraps, 3 Mooncloth and 2 Cured Rugged Hides.\nDesecrated Boots Gluth 0 % in Naxxramas , Gothik the Harvester 0 % in Naxxramas , Instructor Razuvious 0 % in Naxxramas\n12 Wartorn Leather Scrap Skeletal Steed 26.1 % in Naxxramas , Necro Knight Guardian 26.1 % in Naxxramas , Infectious Ghoul 24.5 % in Naxxramas , Stoneskin Gargoyle 24.1 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\n3 Mooncloth\n2 Cured Rugged Hide","desc":"Many heroes fell in the last war and many continue to perish at the hands of the Scourge to this day. From the corpses of the fallen, the armor is stripped and taken back to Naxxramas to be used for unknown purposes.\nRecover the desecrated armor and wartorn armor scraps and supply to me the other material components I require and I will craft Dreamwalker armor.","rew":"You will receive:\nDreamwalker Boots\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"The material cost is high, but soon forgotten.","done":"Your Dreamwalker Boots are ready, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.4,"y":49.3,"n":"Rayne","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"5730":{"id":5730,"t":"Hidden Enemies","lv":16,"min":9,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Thrall in Orgrimmar and tell him what you've learned.","desc":"You are one of my lieutenants! Prepare yourself, ‹class›. I will call upon you soon.\nMy time spent on the Searing Blade may be all but wasted now, but that does not mean that the Shadow Council's schemes elsewhere must suffer. I will do what I can to minimize the damage here in Ragefire Chasm. In the meantime, I will have my agents in the Barrens and Ashenvale begin work on our newest agenda. Return to me soon.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nKris of Orgrimmar Hammer of Orgrimmar Axe of Orgrimmar Staff of Orgrimmar\nExperience: 1,450\n+150 reputation with Orgrimmar","done":"Ashenvale? Hmm, I had not heard of any presence of the Council or the Burning Blade in Ashenvale. My spies will investigate, ‹name›. You have done well.\nFor now, rest, and keep yourself occupied with other tasks. I will call upon you again soon.\nLok-Tar Ogar!","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":49.5,"y":50.6,"n":"Neeru Fireblade","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":31.7,"y":37.8,"n":"Thrall","e":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"9010":{"id":9010,"t":"Saving the Best for Last","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Give Mokvar your Shadowcraft Cap and Shadowcraft Tunic.\nShadowcraft Cap Darkmaster Gandling 0 %\nShadowcraft Tunic General Drakkisath 0 %","desc":"A truly amazing story, ‹name›! You have my thanks, and the heartfelt gratitude of all who were involved, I can assure you. Through your efforts we are delivered from the mistakes of our past.\nAs to your reward, I believe I have a few things that you have definitely earned and will truly enjoy.","rew":"You will receive:\nDarkmantle Cap Darkmantle Tunic\nExperience: 1,650","back":"As per our deal, are you ready to hand over your Shadowcraft pieces in exchange for your new Darkmantle Cap and Tunic?","done":"I will truly miss you, ‹name›. There is a debt that I owe you, which I may never be able to repay.\nEnjoy your new head and chest armor. May it protect you for a long time to come, and help you to achieve even greater honor!","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":34.9,"y":38.3,"n":"Mokvar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"7490":{"id":7490,"t":"Victory for the Horde","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 9,950 experience instead of 13,250, 0.75 times as much.","obj":"Take the Head of Onyxia to Thrall in Orgrimmar.\nHead of Onyxia Onyxia\nProvided: Head of Onyxia","desc":"You have accomplished the impossible. The brood mother of the Black Dragonflight lies dead at your feet. Take her head and present it to your Warchief.","rew":"Experience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"<Thrall's stoic demeanor changes for a split second when he sees the enormous head of Onyxia. The mighty Doomhammer was nearly unsheathed.>","done":"This is a great victory for the Horde, ‹name›. So many times you have honored your Warchief. It is time for the Warchief to honor you.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":31.7,"y":37.8,"n":"Thrall","e":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"1650":{"id":1650,"t":"The Tome of Valor","lv":23,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Daphne Stilwell in Westfall.","desc":"Good! Your lack of hesitation is a sure sign that you are prepared and eager to test yourself. So be it.\nAt the very ends of Westfall's Longshore, a small house overlooks the ocean. There, a couple lives, the Stilwells. Jordan is an incredible smith, and he's gone to Ironforge to meet with the dwarves for a while. But this has left Daphne, his wife, alone and unprotected.\nReports suggest that the Defias have all but taken over the area, Daphne may need some protection from the villains. Go there.","rew":"Experience: 1,850","done":"Hello, ‹name›. I'm assuming by all that armor and weapon of yours, you're either here to try and take my land, or the Church finally sent someone to help protect me while my Jordan's gone.\nWell, let me introduce myself: I'm Daphne Stilwell. It's a pleasure.\nNow, you're not too late... I've only killed a half dozen of the scum since last sun up. They've been a little slow getting 'round the bend up there, but they probably saw you coming, which means they'll probably be here any minute.\nStormwind City Westfall","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":50.5,"y":47.5,"n":"Duthorian Rall","s":1},{"z":"Westfall","x":41.7,"y":89.2,"n":"Daphne Stilwell","e":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"5650":{"id":5650,"t":"Garments of Darkness","lv":4,"min":5,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Deathguard Kel and heal his wounds using Lesser Heal (Rank 2). Afterwards, grant him Power Word: Fortitude and then return to Dark Cleric Beryl in Brill.\nHeal and fortify Deathguard Kel","desc":"Our power comes from darkness and shadow, ‹name›, but that is not your only role. You have acknowledged that there is merit in knowing the healing arts. This is wise. But before you can know the dark, you must also know the light. And for this, I have a test for you.\nNorth of the cemetery is a wounded Deathguard--Deathguard Kel. He has protected us from gnolls for some time, and needs healing. But, you must also fortify his body before he can return to duty. Do both with your spells, and then return to me.","rew":"You will receive:\nAcolyte's Sacrificial Robes\nExperience: 270","back":"Our powers make us ideal for so many situations, ‹name›. You'll find that no matter what though, our ability to mend wounds and increase the amount of damage our companions can take will always be the most desired talents we have access to. Do not let that dissuade you from pursuing other paths as a ‹class›--you can be effective in many ways. But... if you truly wish to destroy your enemies with magical energy, perhaps the arcane is more to your liking.","done":"You have passed my test with ease. Good.\nSoon, you will be ready to take on more responsibility and that road will lead to darker powers--powers that no ‹class› of another race has.\nTake this robe as a symbol of your station. You have earned it. If you do not wish to wear it, then so be it, you may do with it as you will. I and others like us will always acknowledge you for what you've achieved in our ranks.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":61.6,"y":52.2,"n":"Dark Cleric Beryl","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"130":{"id":130,"t":"Visit the Herbalist","lv":15,"min":12,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with the Redridge Herbalist, Martie Jainrose.","desc":"Before you go back to Darcy, can you bring her some flowers for me? You can get them at the herbalist shop back in Lakeshire, at the west end of town.\nBut when you get the flowers...don't tell the herbalist, Martie, whom they're from, or whom they're for...","rew":"Experience: 270","done":"You need a bouquet of flowers? You haven't been in town very long...have you already found for yourself a sweetheart here?\nI know I shouldn't pry, but it's nice to see that love is in the air... especially in dangerous times like these.","pins":[{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":10.2,"y":71.5,"n":"Guard Parker","s":1},{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":16.8,"y":46.3,"n":"Martie Jainrose","e":1}],"cats":["redridge-mountains"]},"95250":{"id":95250,"t":"Abominable Creatures","lv":21,"min":16,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its experience counts the level 30 build, which halved what dungeon quests give beyond a normal quest.","obj":"Collect the Head of the Baron in the Ruins of Lordaeron and bring it back to Captain Truman.\nHead of the Baron","desc":"What do you want, ‹race›? Can't you see there is a war to be won?\nMy master has already charged into the fray and has ordered me to maintain my post. It has been quite some time, however.\nI doubt you'll survive ten minutes in combat, but if it keeps your simple mind busy, why don't you seek out the Grand Marshal. He is the tallest, most statuesque hero you've ever laid eyes on. You'll know him when you see him.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nMonstrous Cleaver Grave Shroud Slain Baron's Signet\nExperience: 3,900\nStart Captain Truman Ruins of Lordaeron Where to find it He stands just inside the entrance. Level 21 , requires level 16 Difficulty 16 17 19 24 28 Side Alliance Type Dungeon Shareable Yes Quest ID 95250","cats":["ruins-of-lordaeron-dungeon"]},"4450":{"id":4450,"t":"Ledger from Tanaris","lv":46,"min":43,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the copy of Goodsteel's Ledger and then find the items listed in it before seeking Krinkle Goodsteel in Tanaris.\nGoodsteel Ledger Goodsteel Ledger\n20 Solid Crystal Leg Shaft Glassweb Spider 80 %\nOverdue Package Damaged Crate\nGoodsteel's Balanced Flameberge Jarquia","desc":"Oh, you know what? That reminds me.\nYou wanna finish up a little job I took up while I was in Tanaris? It's easy...\nKrinkle Goodsteel in Gadgetzan was lookin' for some stuff found here in Searing Gorge and a few other places. Maybe you could take a look at the list and then bring it all to him?\nI'll just slide his ledger under the door if you're interested. Take that, and the stuff he wants back to him after ya collected it all.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nCharged Lightning Rod Girdle of Reprisal\nExperience: 5,050\n+150 reputation with Gadgetzan","back":"Yes, yes? What can I do for you, ‹race›? I'm awfully busy and have many patrons requesting my services. Perhaps you can speed things up. I don't mean to be rude, but I just don't have the time if I'm to catch up on all my work.","done":"Oh, you've seen fit to do some of the work I requested. Excellent. And here I thought you were going to ask me to craft you something.\nThese are all perfect... and everything's here. Thank you, ‹class›.\nMaybe it wouldn't hurt to reward you some... hmm, what would you find useful.\nSearing Gorge Tanaris Dustwallow Marsh Swamp of Sorrows","pins":[{"z":"Searing Gorge","x":65.6,"y":62.2,"n":"Wooden Outhouse","s":1},{"z":"Tanaris","x":51.5,"y":28.8,"n":"Krinkle Goodsteel","e":1}],"cats":["searing-gorge"]},"8770":{"id":8770,"t":"Target: Hive'Ashi Defenders","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Slay 30 Hive'Ashi Defenders and report back to Commander Mar'alith at Cenarion Hold in Silithus. You must also bring Combat Task Briefing I in order to complete this quest.\nCombat Task Briefing I\nHive'Ashi Defender slain : 0/ 30\nProvided: Combat Task Briefing I","desc":"As the war effort mounts, the silithid presence in the area presents an ever increasing threat to our operations. You've been selected to partake on an assault on Hive'Ashi where your primary target will consist of Hive'Ashi defenders.\nReport back to Commander Mar'alith after your task is completed.","rew":"You will receive:\nCenarion Combat Badge\nExperience: 650\n+50 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"You have something to tell me, ‹class›?","done":"Excellent work, ‹name›. Your diligence is as noteworthy as always.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":49.2,"y":34.2,"n":"Commander Mar'alith","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"450":{"id":450,"t":"A Recipe For Death","lv":15,"min":9,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays 14s instead of 7s. Partly read from what the game server sent.","obj":"Retrieve Apothecary Berard's journal from Pyrewood Village and take it to Apothecary Renferrel at the Sepulcher.\nBerard's Journal Berard's Bookshelf","desc":"You can be of further service to the Royal Apothecary Society, ‹name›.\nWhen Arugal cast his wretched magic on the forest, he cursed one of our most promising members, Apothecary Berard. Now a mindless servant of Arugal, Berard is useless to us. But his findings might prove to be of worth. He was studying an ancient plague that killed off all the aquatic life in Lake Lordamere ages ago.\nRetrieve Berard's Journal from his study in the Pyrewood Village Inn and take it to Apothecary Renferrel.","rew":"Money: 14 0 gold, 14 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,350\n+150 reputation with Undercity","back":"I see you are back, ‹name›.","done":"Apothecary Berard's journal! Why you are quite brave, ‹name›. Now let's see what Berard was up to before he went mad. . .\nUndercity Silverpine Forest","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":48.8,"y":69.3,"n":"Master Apothecary Faranell","s":1},{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":42.8,"y":40.9,"n":"Apothecary Renferrel","e":1}],"cats":["silverpine-forest"]},"530":{"id":530,"t":"A Husband's Revenge","lv":20,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill Valdred Moray.\nBring his hands to Raleigh Andrean in the Undercity.\nValdred's Hands Valdred Moray","desc":"Valdred, once my good friend, was my wife's murderer. Although I am incapable of grieving, I do yearn for revenge. If you kill Valdred and bring me his cursed hands, then I will reward you.\nI last heard he was at the Greymane Wall in southern Silverpine, trying to flee into the kingdom of Gilneas.","rew":"You will receive:\nRing of Scorn\nMoney: 12 0 gold, 12 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,550\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"Do you have those hands, ‹name›?","done":"Ah, good. These hands killed my wife, Deliah. Revenge for her murder was my only care, and you were the instrument of that revenge.\nHere, take the ring you returned earlier. Deliah has been dead to me for so long, her ring is a bauble I no longer care to keep. Instead, I will keep these hands as a remembrance of my friend's betrayal.\nUndercity Silverpine Forest","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":62,"y":42.7,"n":"Raleigh Andrean","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silverpine-forest"]},"1090":{"id":1090,"t":"Gerenzo's Orders","lv":22,"min":17,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays 14s instead of 0.","obj":"Get the mysterious ore from Piznik after he finishes mining it.","desc":"You know, I was once the second most important person here at this site. That all changed when Gerenzo took over. Fired my boss, Ziz Fizziks, and sent me down to work in the mines. Ziz told me to stay here and gather information, though. His new boss will pay us well if we can find out what Gerenzo's plans are.\nAnyways, what I do know is that Gerenzo has ordered large amounts of this gold-green ore to be mined. I can get you a sample to bring to Ziz, but you'll have to watch for patrols while I get it.","rew":"Money: 14 0 gold, 14 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,200\n+150 reputation with Ratchet","done":"Thanks, ‹name›. It was looking a little dicey there for a second and we've probably drawn far too much attention to ourselves.\nThe important part is that we have the ore sample, though, and we should get it to Ziz as soon as possible.","pins":[{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":71.9,"y":60,"n":"Piznik","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stonetalon-mountains"]},"690":{"id":690,"t":"Malin's Request","lv":32,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Skuerto at Refuge Pointe in the Arathi Highlands.","desc":"Greetings, ‹name›. You have the look of an adventurer about you, and I have a task that needs some tending to.\nArchmage Trelane, my original master, fled Stromgarde in the Arathi Highlands not too long ago, and he's asked me to help him in recovering some of the items he left behind.\nThe city fell under siege, and he attempted to defend the Tower of Arathor, but to no avail. I have agents in the Highlands already, but they've requested I send more aid. Are you interested?","rew":"Experience: 1,950\n+75 reputation with Ironforge","done":"So, Malin sent ye? I don't care if Muradin rose up from the dead and whisked ye here on a dragon. I'm busy! Talk to Kryten if you need somethin'.\nStormwind City Arathi Highlands","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":50.5,"y":87.5,"n":"Archmage Malin","s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":46.7,"y":47,"n":"Skuerto","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"1250":{"id":1250,"t":"The Missing Diplomat","lv":33,"min":28,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Mikhail in the Wetlands.","desc":"The Defias didn't pay me well enough to die for their cause. They took the king. Yeah, the king of Stormwind, not some lowly diplomat. He was on his way to Theramore to meet with Jaina Proudmore--it was a big deal apparently, and a big secret. But it's not just the Defias that are involved. They're working with someone. I think they knew this was bigger than them.\nMy part was just to get their man on board the king's ship while it was in the harbor. The guy's name was Hendel. That's all I know. I swear!","rew":"Experience: 270","done":"THE KING?! I mean... the king? The real king? Are you joking? You didn't mention you were looking for the king's kidnappers. I didn't even hear he was missing--that would explain his son being crowned some.\nI'll send word to Elling right away. He'll want to know you're on the trail.\nI would never have guessed Jahn would sell out Stormwind for some lousy coin. Even a rogue's got to have honor when it comes to some things.\nThe key now is to find this Hendel. And I think I can help with that.","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":10.5,"y":60.3,"n":"Tapoke \"Slim\" Jahn","s":1},{"z":"Wetlands","x":10.6,"y":60.8,"n":"Mikhail","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"210":{"id":210,"t":"Krazek's Cookery","lv":37,"min":32,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Krazek's Crock Pot to Krazek the goblin.\nKrazek's Crock Pot\nProvided: Krazek's Crock Pot","desc":"I do most of the cooking at the camp. And it used to be a lot of work, until I bought a mechanical cooking pot from a goblin merchant in Booty Bay. The pot is a wonder! It saved me countless hours...until it broke!\nCan you take the pot back to the goblin for me so he can fix it? His name is Krazek.","rew":"Experience: 1,400\n+50 reputation with Booty Bay\n-250 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","back":"Hello! You brought me something?","done":"Oh I see, it's a Krazek's Crock Pot! An ingenious piece of work, but it can break a spring or throw a gear now and then. Let me see what's wrong with this one...\nAha! Its steam charger is rusted out, it has a cracked knuckle-gasket and its fobulator is missing teeth. I'm surprised the pot could even boil a turnip in this state!\nCan I fix it? Of course I can fix it!\nBut there's a price. Oh yes, there is always a price...","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":37.7,"y":3.3,"n":"Corporal Kaleb","s":1},{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":26.9,"y":77.2,"n":"Krazek","e":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"610":{"id":610,"t":"\"Pretty Boy\" Duncan","lv":39,"min":32,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Get Catelyn's dagger from \"Pretty Boy\" Duncan.\nCatelyn's Blade \"Pretty Boy\" Duncan","desc":"My FATHER sent you? I'd have thought that old codger would have given up on me by now.\nIt wasn't really his fault I ran off, he just shouldn't have expected I'd be willing to live a boring life, reading over musty books and associating with grey-haired, stiff-backed, stuffy mages!\nIf you need my dagger, you'll have to get it back from \"Pretty Boy\" Duncan, one of the Bloodsail Buccaneers. Put something 'tween his shoulders and I'm sure he'll give it up.","rew":"Experience: 2,250\n+100 reputation with Booty Bay\n-500 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","back":"I'd never been beat before, you know, ‹name›? Sure I'd been cut, can't get in a knife fight without that, but he just smacked me on the side of the head, blacked me out. When I came to my blade was gone.\nAs much as my nickname might indicate, I still need a knife to fight, and for me, it has to be that one.","done":"You beat Duncan? I guess you aren't as wet behind the ears as you looked at first glance.\nI suppose that also means I shouldn't challenge you to a fight any time soon!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":27.3,"y":77.5,"n":"Catelyn the Blade","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"7810":{"id":7810,"t":"Arena Master","lv":55,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Short John Mithril in the Stranglethorn Arena.\nProvided: Arena Master","desc":"There must be more to being a master of the arena than this! Perhaps the Pirate who runs the event at Gurubashi will know!","rew":"Experience: 550","done":"Arr Me Hearty! Gaining one Trinket be not enough to make ye master of the Arena! Now tis the time to truly prove your steel.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":29.6,"y":47.4,"n":"Short John Mithril","e":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"930":{"id":930,"t":"The Glowing Fruit","lv":10,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the glowing fruit to Denalan at Lake Al'Ameth.\nGlowing Fruit\nProvided: Glowing Fruit","desc":"Hanging from beneath its fronds of this glowing plant is a large, round fruit.\nDenalan would want to study this fruit, you are certain.","rew":"Money: 3 50 0 gold, 3 silver, 50 copper Experience: 850\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"‹name›, you look like you have something to tell me. Do you have news concerning the timberlings?","done":"You found this on Teldrassil? Intriguing... this fruit is exotic. Perhaps its seeds were brought here from far off. Perhaps even as far as Azeroth! And there's something about this fruit... it seems to have reacted very strangely with the soil of Teldrassil.\nThank you, ‹name›. Now if you'll excuse me, I must study this further...","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":42.6,"y":76.2,"n":"Strange Fruited Plant","s":1},{"z":"Teldrassil","x":60.9,"y":68.5,"n":"Denalan","e":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"5250":{"id":5250,"t":"Starfall","lv":56,"min":53,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 575 experience instead of 850, 0.68 times as much.","obj":"Find Starfall in Winterspring and speak with Wynd Nightchaser.","desc":"In Winterspring, to the north of Felwood, there are many ancient elven ruins. It's a harsh land, but it holds many secrets and places to explore.\nMy studies here keep me so busy that I have not had the opportunity to travel to Winterspring for some time. But there's no reason why you shouldn't travel there and study the ruins.\nWhile you're there, look for Wynd Nightchaser. He spends most of his time in Starfall and he knows a lot about the area.\nTell him that you are a student of mine...","rew":"Experience: 575\n+10 reputation with Darnassus","done":"A student of Daryn Lightwind? Nice to meet you, ‹name›.\nTeldrassil Winterspring","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":55.4,"y":92.2,"n":"Daryn Lightwind","s":1},{"z":"Winterspring","x":52,"y":30.4,"n":"Wynd Nightchaser","e":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"850":{"id":850,"t":"Kolkar Leaders","lv":16,"min":11,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Barak's Head to Regthar Deathgate, west of the Crossroads.\nKodobane's Head Barak Kodobane","desc":"The centaurs have plagued the Tauren for years. And recently, the Kolkar centaurs of the Barrens have grown into a real threat. Normally they were disorganized in these lands, but new leaders have risen among them. Rallying them.\nTo preserve our holdings here, these centaur leaders must be destroyed.\nBring me the head of Barak Kodobane. He camps near the Forgotten Pools to the north.\nDefeat him, then return to me.","rew":"Money: 8 0 gold, 8 silver, 0 copper Experience: 875\n+75 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Hello, ‹name›. Do you have Barak's Head for me?","done":"Well done, ‹name›. The centaur are low, brutish creatures, but a few have the wit and vision to lead. And those are the most dangerous.\nBarak was such a centaur. It is good that he is dead.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":45.3,"y":28.4,"n":"Regthar Deathgate","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"97250":{"id":97250,"t":"Wrongly blamed justly corrected","lv":23,"min":18,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Slay Alliance soldiers encroaching into the Barrens at the border to Dustwallow Marsh, then return to Grunt Logmar at Camp Taurajo.\nEncroaching Soldier slain : 0/ 2\nOutraged Pillager slain","desc":"Traveler, have you plans to head toward Dustwallow Marsh? I have heard mutterings that a few human soldiers have taken a stand at its border and are toppling the landmarks left behind by our tauren pathfinders.\nRumor has it that a favored tavern has burned to the ground, and in typical Alliance fashion, they immediately cast their blame onto the Horde! I cannot know whether there is any truth to their claim, but their incursion onto OUR land must not stand.\nKill first, investigate later!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nEncroacher's Claim Pathfinder's Clearway Traveler's Shawl\nMoney: 30 0 gold, 30 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,300","done":"So the rumors were true! I expected as much, tensions have been rising along the eastern coast for some time. I knew it would only be a matter of time before conflict crept into our territory.\nHowever, I am skeptical that we played a role in the tavern's destruction. Too many Horde civilians rely on that route for trade and travel. Perhaps you could investigate further if you find the time.\nIn any case, today's deed is a victory for the Horde, and a stern warning to the Alliance!\nThe Barrens Dustwallow Marsh","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":44.6,"y":59.2,"n":"Grunt Logmar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"4770":{"id":4770,"t":"Homeward Bound","lv":29,"min":25,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Escort Pao'ka Swiftmountain from Highperch, and then talk to Motega Firemane in Whitereach Post.","desc":"Please help me, ‹class›! I've been hiding here in Highperch for some time now and it's been days since I've seen a friendly face. I came here to study the wyvern and I think I got a little too close. After being chased away from one of the nests I got lost.\nI need to get back to Whitereach Post! Motega does not know that I am missing and will be furious to know that I ventured into Highperch by myself.\nWhitereach Post is just east of here... please take me there!","rew":"Money: 19 0 gold, 19 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,350\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","done":"Whats! If I knew that Pao'ka Swiftmountain was going to snoop around Highperch, I would have chained him to a totem! His father was reluctant allowing him to come with me to Thousand Needles. We came here to study the different creatures that inhabit these beautiful lands.\nI appreciate the help you have shown Pao'ka. I hope this covers any misfortunes this deed has cost you.","pins":[{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":17.9,"y":40.6,"n":"Pao'ka Swiftmountain","s":1},{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":21.5,"y":32.3,"n":"Motega Firemane","e":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"370":{"id":370,"t":"At War With The Scarlet Crusade","lv":9,"min":5,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Executor Zygand in Brill wants you to kill Captain Perrine, 3 Scarlet Zealots and 3 Scarlet Missionaries.\nCaptain Perrine slain\nScarlet Zealot slain : 0/ 3\nScarlet Missionary slain : 0/ 3","desc":"The strategic documents from Executor Arren contain all the details we need to wipe the human infestation from the lands. According to the information, The Scarlet Crusade has assigned Captain Perrine and a brigade to the ruined tower southwest of Brill.\nKill Perrine along with 3 Zealots and 3 Missionaries and report back to me.","rew":"Money: 3 0 gold, 3 silver, 0 copper Experience: 775\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"Young ‹class›, you shouldn't be wasting your time here in Brill when your people need you fighting for their cause. Now, take up arms and travel to the southwest, to the ruined tower, and slay Captain Perrine along with 3 Scarlet Zealots and 3 Scarlet Missionaries. We shall herd the Scarlet Crusade like cattle to their demise.","done":"Captain Perrine's death will undoubtedly please The Dark Lady. You have performed your duty well, ‹class›.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":60.6,"y":51.8,"n":"Executor Zygand","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"4290":{"id":4290,"t":"The Fare of Lar'korwi","lv":53,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find the carcass of Lar'korwi's freshest kill and steal a Piece of Threshadon Carcass before returning to Torwa Pathfinder in Un'Goro Crater.\nPiece of Threshadon Carcass Fresh Threshadon Carcass","desc":"Once, a long time ago, a brother of mine took some meat from one of Lar'korwi's kills. He didn't know it at the time, but Lar'korwi saw him from the forest. Lar'korwi followed my brother for days, destroying everything he touched. My brother, scared, finally decided to run from the Crater and leave Lar'korwi behind.\nLar'korwi killed him not far from this spot.\nIf you want to provoke Lar'korwi, find a fresh kill of his and take some of the meat from it.\nReturn to me afterwards.","rew":"Experience: 5,250","back":"Do not take my words lightly, ‹name›. If you truly wish to face this creature, then you must be careful... and smart. It will take a great deal of strength and insight to draw out Lar'korwi and defeat him.","done":"This will do nicely, ‹name›. It seems Lar'korwi eats well these days. Although, I wonder where he found a threshadon in this area. Odd.\nRegardless, I will hold onto this until you are ready for your confrontation with the beast. Do not worry for my safety--I am sure you've angered Lar'korwi enough that he will not kill me until after he's tasted your flesh.","pins":[{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":71.6,"y":76,"n":"Torwa Pathfinder","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ungoro-crater"]},"3570":{"id":3570,"t":"Seeping Corruption","lv":52,"min":45,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"Money: 75 0 gold, 75 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,100\n+100 reputation with Undercity","done":"I never dreamed the elixir would take hold that quickly. Thank you, ‹name›. I will get to work on the rest of these samples right away. I'm sure they'll be usable by the Lady Sylvanas and the Forsaken soon enough.","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":48.7,"y":71.4,"n":"Chemist Cuely","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["undercity"]},"1490":{"id":1490,"t":"Nara Wildmane","lv":16,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 10 instead of 12.","obj":"Speak with Nara Wildmane.","desc":"I entered the land of dreams, and dreamed of a cult of druids who dwell in the Wailing Caverns. I saw that their goals were once noble, but they have lost their way. They are now servants of the taint seeping through the Barrens.\nI am old and my strength fails. I could not long dwell in that dreaming place and know little more of the tainted druids. But Nara is young and her spirit is fierce. She remained in the dreaming when I fled.\nSpeak with Nara. She is in the tent, over yonder.","rew":"Experience: 120\n+10 reputation with Thunder Bluff","done":"Yes, it is true. I know of the druids in the Wailing Caverns. I have seen their twisted, scaled faces. I know their crimes, and I know their plans.\nYou must stop them, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":78.6,"y":28.6,"n":"Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":75.6,"y":31.6,"n":"Nara Wildmane","e":1}],"cats":["wailing-caverns"]},"3090":{"id":3090,"t":"Tainted Parchment","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Read the Tainted Parchment and speak to Nartok inside the Den in the Valley of Trials.\nTainted Parchment\nProvided: Tainted Parchment","desc":"Ah, while you were gone a parchment came for you, ‹name›.\nI usually avoid dealing with warlocks if I can help it, but I think you should read it when you have time. If I'm not mistaken, it came from your newly-appointed trainer Nartok. He would have words with you when you're ready.","rew":"Experience: 40\n+50 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Finally, you've arrived... and discretely also. Good.\nOur world is full of fools, ‹name›. Even the mighty Thrall has greater flaws than most can see. He turns his back on the power needed to make this land ours completely! We're not the same people who were manipulated and used by creatures from the Nether. We are our own people. We are proud... and we are strong.","done":"And now you've joined our ranks also. Don't misunderstand, ‹name›. Just because you have access to power that many will be jealous of, it does not mean you will be accepted easily. Thrall allows our kind into Orgrimmar because we are still his fellow kin--he cannot turn his back on us, or we would become as pathetic as the humans who enslaved him. My point is: be careful. You can be powerful, but if you are foolish, then you are as good dead.\nIf you need training in spells then return to me.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":42.1,"y":68.3,"n":"Gornek","s":1},{"z":"Durotar","x":40.7,"y":68.5,"n":"Nartok","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"8290":{"id":8290,"t":"Vanquish the Invaders","lv":15,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 1,050 experience instead of 10,500, 0.1 times as much.","obj":"Enter Warsong Gulch and defeat the Horde, obtain a Warsong Gulch Mark of Honor, and return to Sentinel Farsong at the Silverwing Grove.\nWarsong Gulch Mark of Honor","desc":"Beyond this tunnel you will find a field of strife and turmoil, young ‹class›. The Horde continue to decimate our sacred forest, cutting down the evergreen foliage to power their machines of war.\nEnter Warsong Gulch and defend Silverwing Hold. Push back the invading Horde forces!\nDo this, and earn a talisman of merit. Bring me such a talisman, ‹name›, and I shall reward you.","rew":"Money: 20 0 gold, 20 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,050\n+200 reputation with Silverwing Sentinels\nLevel 15 , requires level 10 Difficulty 10 11 13 18 22 Side Human, Dwarf, Night Elf, Gnome Type PvP Shareable No Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8290","cats":["warsong-gulch"]},"50":{"id":50,"t":"Sweet Amber","lv":44,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Grimbooze Thunderbrew wants Truesilver.\nTruesilver Bar Felsteel Chest 8.6 % , Heavy Fel Iron Chest 5.1 % , Adamantite Bound Chest 5.1 % , Solid Chest 0 % and 4 more","desc":"I'll mix and mix till we have a mash\nFor this will be our own private stash\nA still must be fashioned of metal strong\nBring me some Truesilver so I can finish this song.","rew":"Money: 1 25 1 gold, 25 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,650","back":"An encore for you? Well sure friend!\nI'll mix and mix till we have a mash\nFor this will be our own private stash\nA still must be fashioned of metal strong\nBring me some Truesilver so I can finish this song.","done":"Hiccup! Ho ho!","pins":[{"z":"Westfall","x":44.6,"y":80.3,"n":"Grimbooze Thunderbrew","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["westfall"]},"290":{"id":290,"t":"Lifting the Curse","lv":30,"min":22,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Get the Intrepid Strongbox Key from Captain Halyndor.\nUse the key to open the Intrepid's Locked Strongbox.\nIntrepid Strongbox Key Captain Halyndor","desc":"To break the curse and free all of my brethren, the...thing...stowed on my ship must be retrieved and cleansed! I don't know what it was, but I do know that it was stored securely in the ship's strongbox, which Captain Halyndor lorded over.\nMy old captain is still in my dreams. I know he walks my doomed ship, the Intrepid. Get the key from him, and use it to open the Intrepid's strongbox.\nThen, after you have the cursed thing, bring it to the priest Glorin Steelbrow in town.","rew":"Experience: 1,200\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","back":"This chest is securely locked.","done":"The key is rusted but it fits the lock neatly.","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":10.9,"y":59.6,"n":"First Mate Fitzsimmons","s":1},{"z":"Wetlands","x":14.4,"y":24,"n":"Intrepid's Locked Strongbox","e":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"92850":{"id":92850,"t":"The missing scholar","lv":10,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Slay the Shriekling Matriarch in the Shriekling Den then return its head to Fillion Flamebreeze in Valanaar.\nShriekling Matriarch's Head","desc":"I am feeling much better already. I have some skill with the arcane arts and we are but a short distance from Valanaar. I can make it on my own. More important than my safety however is how close to Valanaar these shrieklings have nested and the danger they pose. If you would be so kind, please head back inside and take the head of that beast!\nAfter it's done, you'll find me back in Valanaar. I need to report to the Supreme Magister what occurred here and the status of my mission.","rew":"Money: 7 0 gold, 7 silver, 0 copper Experience: 850\n+100 reputation with High Order","back":"That fool Fillion...","done":"Well, I confess that I am intensely relieved that Fillion has returned to us. He never was good at minding his surroundings. Always too busy lost in thought, or with his nose in a book.\nThank you, ‹class›.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":52,"y":69.4,"n":"Fillion Flamebreeze","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":66.2,"y":79.8,"n":"Dondallion Whisperwind","e":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":66.2,"y":79.8,"n":"Fillion Flamebreeze","e":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"93090":{"id":93090,"t":"What comes next","lv":13,"min":7,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Ayessa Dawnsinger when you are prepared to leave Zephras Isle.","desc":"Please extend my thanks to Ayessa for all that the Windshapers and your new friends from this \"Earthen Ring\" have done for Zephras Isle. I'm aware of the plan to take the Windshapers shamans and leave the island, and your order has my blessing and well-wishes in this expedition.\nI can only hope that whatever solution the Windshapers find can truly provide us with the stability we've lacked these past years.\nWinds be with you, ‹name›.","done":"I'm pleased to hear that we have High Elder Shadowsong's blessing for our expedition. Now that the cult has been defeated and preparations have been made, I think it's finally time.\nMuln has worked diligently to help us get stable skycutter transport going between Zephras Isle and a place called Mulgore, where the Earthen Ring make their home. We've been doing test voyages and some of our people are already waiting on the other side.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":66.2,"y":76.6,"n":"Talaanis Shadowsong","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":59,"y":79.6,"n":"Ayessa Dawnsinger","e":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"2770":{"id":2770,"t":"Gahz'rilla","lv":50,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Gahz'rilla's Electrified Scale to Wizzle Brassbolts in the Shimmering Flats.\nGahz'rilla's Electrified Scale Gahz'rilla","desc":"Deep in Zul'Farrak, the sand troll city in Tanaris, there is a sacred pool. From that pool the trolls summon a huge beast! Gahz'rilla! He's so fierce that even his scales crackle with energy. It's that energy I want to harness for my car!\nBring me the electrified scale of Gahz'rilla!\nBut the summoning of Gahz'rilla is a well-kept secret of the trolls. To face him, you must first wrest the secret from them.","rew":"You will receive:\nCarrot on a Stick\nMoney: 75 0 gold, 75 silver, 0 copper Experience: 7,100","back":"Do you have the scale? I can't wait to try different ways to harness its energy!","done":"Wow, you got the scale! Thanks, ‹name›. I can't wait to get to work on this thing!\nSo you saw Gahz'rilla? Was he as big as they say??","pins":[{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":78.1,"y":77.1,"n":"Wizzle Brassbolts","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zulfarrak"]},"8050":{"id":8050,"t":"The Eye of Zuldazar","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60.","obj":"The Eye of Zuldazar","rew":"You will receive:\nThe Eye of Zuldazar\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"Tales of your battles against the Gurubashi are whispered in the winds, priestess. Even royalty is beginning to talk of your deeds. It is rumored that King Rastakhan even mentioned you by name.\nThe time has come to imbue the Eye. Hand me the talisman and I shall perform the service.","done":"Be resolute in your endeavors, ‹name›. The Soulflayer will attempt to siphon your will to live.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":15.3,"y":16.1,"n":"Al'tabim the All-Seeing","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zulgurub"]}});